WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.105 --> 00:00:01.909
(atmospheric music)

00:00:01.909 --> 00:00:05.409
- Imagine a river, hot enough to kill you,

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:10.644
said to be the home of a powerful

00:00:10.644 --> 00:00:12.627
Amazonian water spirit.

00:00:12.627 --> 00:00:15.851
That place is real, and I've been there.

00:00:15.851 --> 00:00:20.018
It’s the Shanay-timpishka, the
boiling river of the Amazon.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.710
(lively music)

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.735
My name's Andrés Ruzo, and I'm a geothermal

00:00:30.735 --> 00:00:33.623
scientist and conservationist.

00:00:33.623 --> 00:00:35.409
As a boy in Lima, my grandfather told me

00:00:35.409 --> 00:00:37.327
this crazy story about the search

00:00:37.327 --> 00:00:38.720
for the lost city of gold.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:39.553
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:39.553 --> 00:00:41.342
But there was a detail in that story,

00:00:41.342 --> 00:00:43.069
about a river that boiled.

00:00:43.069 --> 00:00:43.957
I certainly imagined it,

00:00:43.957 --> 00:00:46.289
but never really dwelled on it,

00:00:46.289 --> 00:00:47.949
it was just a detail.

00:00:47.949 --> 00:00:49.306
It's getting much hotter.

00:00:49.306 --> 00:00:51.973
It turns out this place is real.

00:00:55.564 --> 00:00:56.770
So the boiling river's located

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:58.172
in the heart of the
central Peruvian Amazon.

00:00:58.172 --> 00:01:00.211
(bubbling water)

00:01:00.211 --> 00:01:01.712
The hottest temperature I've measured

00:01:01.712 --> 00:01:04.896
was over 210 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:01:04.896 --> 00:01:06.981
To put that into everyday terms,

00:01:06.981 --> 00:01:10.647
the average coffee is roughly 130 degrees.

00:01:10.647 --> 00:01:12.999
It's hard to physically imagine

00:01:12.999 --> 00:01:14.343
that much hot water.

00:01:14.343 --> 00:01:16.359
You stick your hand in, and you will see

00:01:16.359 --> 00:01:18.118
second and third degree burns

00:01:18.118 --> 00:01:20.035
in a matter of seconds.

00:01:22.955 --> 00:01:25.275
I've seen a number of animals fall

00:01:25.275 --> 00:01:26.586
into the boiling river,

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.774
everything from birds to reptiles.

00:01:28.774 --> 00:01:29.607
(falling water)

00:01:29.607 --> 00:01:31.015
Complex organisms like us,

00:01:31.015 --> 00:01:32.920
we don't do well at
those high temperatures.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.801
We literally start to cook on the bone.

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:37.583
Feeling that heat come into you,

00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:39.465
breathing in this thick hot air,

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:41.273
where you can feel the air

00:01:41.273 --> 00:01:42.818
heating you up inside your nose,

00:01:42.818 --> 00:01:43.889
you can feel it going into your lungs,

00:01:43.889 --> 00:01:46.129
you can feel the presence of your lungs

00:01:46.129 --> 00:01:48.552
because of the heat of the air.

00:01:48.552 --> 00:01:51.788
It still gives me goosebumps.

00:01:51.788 --> 00:01:54.068
The true name of the boiling river

00:01:54.068 --> 00:01:56.985
is Shanay-timpishka and that means,

00:01:57.923 --> 00:01:59.625
according to one of the local shamans,

00:01:59.625 --> 00:02:02.449
boiled with the heat of the sun.

00:02:02.449 --> 00:02:04.193
It's spectacular.

00:02:04.193 --> 00:02:05.689
This place has totally redefined

00:02:05.689 --> 00:02:08.522
what it means to be sacred for me.

00:02:11.265 --> 00:02:12.816
I think once you've experienced something

00:02:12.816 --> 00:02:14.265
that's truly moved you,

00:02:14.265 --> 00:02:15.859
you love it.

00:02:15.859 --> 00:02:18.026
And you can't let that go.

